Body:
Not sure what the issue is, but I am experiencing this quite heavily when using subagents with GHCP as a provider. Primary agents are not that often affected - for whatever reason.  (EDIT: Reason might be, that I am creating large plans using subagents, and the thinking with Opus takes to long. Opus is not displaying thinking tokens )

Today rolling back isn't a valid option for me. I got some sessions not finished and dont want to loose history therefore.

These permanent DB migrations are annoying and sort of dangerous. Not the first time this year that an update couldnt be rolled back. Maybe there is a need of DB backups before migration and a documented and defined way of rolling back???

This is an absolute pain for professional work with near deadlines. I'll never will run an spontaneous update again.

EDIT#2: Adding the long timeout for GHCP as Opus Provider solved the issue for me - at least in this moment.  Seems that the delay between chunks has become too long, because the thinking tokens are now completely hidden.

```
  "provider": {
    "github-copilot": {
      "options": {
        "timeout": 600000,
        "chunkTimeout": 600000
      }
    }
  }

```
